  "summary": "Reverse shell to hardcoded IP on require",
  "details": "The gem's library entry point opens a TCPSocket to the hardcoded remote host 66.78.40.218:32768, reopens STDIN, STDOUT, and STDERR onto that socket, and execs /bin/sh -i. Any `require \"zzhelloworld_socktest\"` yields an interactive remote shell on the installing host to whoever controls that endpoint, with no authentication, no disclosure, and no user interaction. The behavior fires automatically at load time with full-host RCE blast radius.",
